  "raw_response": "Looking at the examples, I can identify the pattern:\n\n1. Each connected component of non-zero cells has a **body** (most common color) and **seed cells** (other colors adjacent to the body's corner)\n2. The **corner** is the body cell with the most non-body neighbors\n3. Each seed's direction relative to the corner determines a reflection:\n   - Horizontal neighbor \u2192 reflect body horizontally\n   - Vertical neighbor \u2192 reflect body vertically  \n   - Diagonal neighbor \u2192 reflect both ways\n4. Reflected copies use the seed's color\n\n```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    import copy\n    from collections import deque, Counter\n\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    result = copy.deepcopy(grid)\n    visited = [[False]*cols for _ in range(rows)]\n\n    def bfs(sr, sc):\n        q = deque([(sr, sc)])\n        visited[sr][sc] = True\n        cells = [(sr, sc)]\n        while q:\n            r, c = q.popleft()\n            for dr in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                for dc in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                    if dr == 0 and dc == 0: continue\n                    nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n                    if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] != 0:\n                        visited[nr][nc] = True\n                        q.append((nr, nc))\n                        cells.append((nr, nc))\n        return cells\n\n    components = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0 and not visited[r][c]:\n                components.append(bfs(r, c))\n\n    for comp in components:\n        color_counts = Counter(grid[r][c] for r, c in comp)\n        body_color = color_counts.most_common(1)[0][0]\n        body_cells = [(r, c) for r, c in comp if grid[r][c] == body_color]\n        non_body_set = set((r, c) for r, c in comp if grid[r][c] != body_color)\n\n        best_corner = None\n        best_count = 0\n        for r, c in body_cells:\n            count = sum(1 for dr in [-1,0,1] for dc in [-1,0,1]\n                       if (dr or dc) and (r+dr, c+dc) in non_body_set)\n            if count > best_count:\n                best_count = count\n                best_corner = (r, c)\n\n        if best_corner is None:\n            continue\n\n        cr, cc = best_corner\n        for dr in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            for dc in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                if dr == 0 and dc == 0: continue\n                nr, nc = cr+dr, cc+dc\n                if (nr, nc) in non_body_set:\n                    seed_color = grid[nr][nc]\n                    mid_r = (cr + nr) / 2.0\n                    mid_c = (cc + nc) / 2.0\n                    for br, bc in body_cells:\n                        if dr != 0 and dc != 0:\n                            new_r, new_c = int(2*mid_r - br), int(2*mid_c - bc)\n                        elif dr != 0:\n                            new_r, new_c = int(2*mid_r - br), bc\n                        else:\n                            new_r, new_c = br, int(2*mid_c - bc)\n                        if 0 <= new_r < rows and 0 <= new_c < cols:\n                            result[new_r][new_c] = seed_color\n\n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    import copy\n    from collections import deque, Counter\n\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    result = copy.deepcopy(grid)\n    visited = [[False]*cols for _ in range(rows)]\n\n    def bfs(sr, sc):\n        q = deque([(sr, sc)])\n        visited[sr][sc] = True\n        cells = [(sr, sc)]\n        while q:\n            r, c = q.popleft()\n            for dr in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                for dc in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                    if dr == 0 and dc == 0: continue\n                    nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n                    if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] != 0:\n                        visited[nr][nc] = True\n                        q.append((nr, nc))\n                        cells.append((nr, nc))\n        return cells\n\n    components = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0 and not visited[r][c]:\n                components.append(bfs(r, c))\n\n    for comp in components:\n        color_counts = Counter(grid[r][c] for r, c in comp)\n        body_color = color_counts.most_common(1)[0][0]\n        body_cells = [(r, c) for r, c in comp if grid[r][c] == body_color]\n        non_body_set = set((r, c) for r, c in comp if grid[r][c] != body_color)\n\n        best_corner = None\n        best_count = 0\n        for r, c in body_cells:\n            count = sum(1 for dr in [-1,0,1] for dc in [-1,0,1]\n                       if (dr or dc) and (r+dr, c+dc) in non_body_set)\n            if count > best_count:\n                best_count = count\n                best_corner = (r, c)\n\n        if best_corner is None:\n            continue\n\n        cr, cc = best_corner\n        for dr in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            for dc in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                if dr == 0 and dc == 0: continue\n                nr, nc = cr+dr, cc+dc\n                if (nr, nc) in non_body_set:\n                    seed_color = grid[nr][nc]\n                    mid_r = (cr + nr) / 2.0\n                    mid_c = (cc + nc) / 2.0\n                    for br, bc in body_cells:\n                        if dr != 0 and dc != 0:\n                            new_r, new_c = int(2*mid_r - br), int(2*mid_c - bc)\n                        elif dr != 0:\n                            new_r, new_c = int(2*mid_r - br), bc\n                        else:\n                            new_r, new_c = br, int(2*mid_c - bc)\n                        if 0 <= new_r < rows and 0 <= new_c < cols:\n                            result[new_r][new_c] = seed_color\n\n    return result",
